course: dictionary
lesson: 15383
title: Specified: named clearly and exactly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Specified» is the past form of the verb «specify», which means to say or state something clearly and exactly. When a rule has been specified, it has been named clearly, so nobody has to guess.
explain: «Specified» can also be an adjective. «Please arrive at the specified time» means at the exact time that has already been fixed, not any time you like. Look for clues around the word, such as «the» or a number, which often tell you something has been fixed in advance.
explain: «Write your answer in the specified box» tells you there is one box, chosen beforehand, and you must use it. «Unless otherwise specified» means «unless it says something different». Try swapping in «named clearly» or «fixed in advance» and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Specify» means to state something clearly and exactly.
fact: «Specified» is the past form of «specify», and it is also used as an adjective.
fact: «Specified» as an adjective means named or fixed clearly in advance, as in «a specified amount».
fact: In maths, «the specified unit» is the exact unit the question asks for, such as metres or grams.
fact: Rules and forms often give specified times, prices and sizes, so you know exactly what is needed.
exercise: «Please bring the specified amount of money to the shop.» What does specified mean here? | Lost or missing | Very large and heavy | Tasty and cold | *Named clearly and fixed in advance
exercise: The teacher said, «Write your answer in the specified box.» Which box must you use? | The box nearest the door | *A box chosen and named in advance | A box made of card | Any box you like
exercise: Find and copy the one word from this sentence that is a past form of «specify»: «The rules were specified in the letter.» | letter | rules | the | *specified
test: «The recipe gives the specified temperature for the oven.» What does specified mean? | Hot and smoky | Broken and useless | Hard to find | *Named exactly and fixed in advance
test: In maths, what is «the specified unit»? | A unit that is always wrong | The longest unit on the list | Any unit you like | *The exact unit the question asks for
exam: «Unless otherwise specified, the lunch money is due on Monday.» What does «unless otherwise specified» mean? | Unless you are very tired | Only if it is raining | *Unless it says something different | Until the end of the year
